{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>From a month old and upward you shall count them.</b> They said in the Midrash: this is what the verse says (Psalms 92:13): ״צדיק כתמר יפרח״ — 'the righteous flourishes like a palm tree.' Just as this palm tree casts its shade from afar, so too the reward of the righteous is distant. Just as it produces dates and it produces inferior fruits, so too among Israel there are men of Torah and there are ignoramuses. Just as it produces inferior fruits that do not enter the storehouse, and it has dates that do enter the storehouse, so too Israel in the wilderness — some of them entered the land of Israel and some of them did not enter."], :book :numbers, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:29:59.671507821Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}